217-  1. [Replace Python-specific tool with TypeScript equivalent] Test runner and version (pytest replacement) → Vitest 4 (^4.1.10, current stable major; do not adopt 5.0 beta) with @vitest/coverage-v8 at the same version, node environment, no globals
218-  2. [Adapt existing repo decision] Test structure: test/ vs colocated → Top-level tests/ directory mirroring concerns (tests/config.test.ts, api.test.ts, cli.test.ts) plus tests/integration/ subprocess tier; unit/integration script split
219-  3. [Adapt existing repo decision] Coverage provider, thresholds, and exclusions → v8 provider, coverage.include ['src/**/*.ts'] (required in v4), thresholds lines 95 / functions 95 / branches 90 / statements 95 enforced in CI, only thin I/O adapter/entry files excluded with explanatory comments; local fast loop stays coverage-free
220-  4. [Replace Python-specific tool with TypeScript equivalent] CLI smoke-test approach (CliRunner replacement) → Two tiers: in-process runCli(argv, deps) -> exit code with injected deps asserting exit codes and separated stdout/stderr; plus tests/integration/ spawning the built dist CLI via subprocess with staleness-aware globalSetup rebuild and cli-standards R9.14 conformance fixtures
221-  5. [Adapt existing repo decision] Mocking seams and fixture patterns → DI-first (fakes/vi.fn spies passed through the deps object; injected fetchImpl as the only HTTP transport seam), vi.stubEnv for env, fs.mkdtemp for temp files, local factory helpers instead of global setup; vi.mock reserved as last resort; fix the source's latent mis-mock bug rather than porting it and add missing exit-3/exit-4 tests
222-  6. [Keep source Python repo cross-platform tool] Relaxed lint/type rules for the test tree → Carry per-glob overrides for tests/** (asserts allowed, looser ergonomics) with explanatory comments; tests stay under strict tsconfig but excluded from build output; exact rule IDs owned by the lint topic (T04) — stated dependency, not decided here
